{"ticket_id":103,"agent":"accounting","note":"Accounting review — shop date 2026-08-31. Request is for 20 units of CC-HOOD-NAVY, size M, for Yale AI Club. Pricing evidence: list price $58/unit, unit cost $22/unit; list gross margin is $36/unit (62.07%), or $720 total before any replenishment/shipping costs. Current stock is 8 units, leaving a 12-unit shortfall; the only matched vendor, Bulldog Print Co, has a 5-day lead time and shipping is blocked by an open invoice whose ID/amount/payment status were not returned. No customer invoice or payment obligation is linked to ticket 103, so no payment request is supported or prepared.

Illustrative discount options for all 20 units, before unreturned replenishment/shipping costs: 5% = $55.10/unit, $33.10/unit margin, $662 total gross margin; 10% = $52.20/unit, $30.20/unit margin, $604 total; 15% = $49.30/unit, $27.30/unit margin, $546 total; 20% = $46.40/unit, $24.40/unit margin, $488 total. Each remains above the returned $22 unit cost, but the true safe floor cannot be finalized until the 12-unit replenishment cost and shipping are confirmed. Recommend treating 20% as the maximum provisional discount, subject to confirmation of replenishment economics; do not promise 20-unit immediate fulfillment, and consider an 8-unit in-stock offer or contingent fulfillment for the remaining 12.

Human approvals/decisions required: approve the price override/discount and fulfillment terms; Boss must decide whether to pursue the blocked vendor and authorize any supported invoice payment after accounting verifies the exact open invoice and checking cash. Vendor shipping block and 5-day lead time remain visible. Ticket stays open; this note is recommendation-only and no payment was executed.","close_ticket":false}
